# The suite plays this against the server, a section per connection:
# a line "> text" is sent, "< text" is the reply expected back, and a
# section ends when the server closes the connection. The last line
# stops the server, whose standard output is then compared with
# 03-cache-server.out.

# A miss, a set, a hit, the errors, then QUIT.
> GET answer
< MISSING
> SET answer 42
< OK
> GET answer
< 42
>
< ERR empty line
> SET answer
< ERR usage: SET key value
> GET
< ERR usage: GET key
> FROB answer
< ERR unknown command
> QUIT

# A second connection sees the first's entry: the store outlives a
# connection. SHUTDOWN closes this one and stops the server.
> GET answer
< 42
> SET greeting hello
< OK
> SHUTDOWN
